	)
	(text "The differential Ethernet signals should be routed as 100Ω differential pairs, with suitable clearances. Length matching\nbetween pairs should be better than 50mm, so in the typical case no length matching is required. However the signals\nwithin a pair need to be length matched, ideally to better than 0.15mm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 245.11 289.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0dfaa66d-1f7e-4905-b90d-d621be2e7fed")
	)
	(text "PWR LED"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 444.5 363.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0f0ed7c1-f916-4ab7-830d-d57b24a2e9a7")
	)
	(text "M.2 Socket 3 (M-Key) PCIe x1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 478.028 198.628 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "167bd1ff-cadc-4481-871b-55a10f14554b")
	)
	(text "ROUTING:\n* HDMI signals should be routed as 100Ω differential pairs. Each signal within a pair should ideally be matched to better\nthan 0.15mm. Pairs don't typically need any extra matching, as they only have to be matched to 25mm\n* USB: The differential pair should be routed as a 90Ω differential\npair. The length of the P/N signals should ideally be matched to better than 0.15mm.\n* PCIE: The differential PCIe signals should be routed as 90Ω differential pairs, with suitable clearances. There is no need to\nmatch the lengths between pairs, only the signals within a Pair need to be length matched ideally to better than 0.1mm.\n* ENTHERNET: The differential Ethernet signals should be routed as 100Ω differential pairs, with suitable clearances. Length matching\nbetween pairs should be better than 50mm, so in the typical case no length matching is required. However the signals\nwithin a pair need to be length matched, ideally to better than 0.15mm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 594.36 107.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1e5da6a3-75af-4553-aea2-560c3273bcba")
	)
